# Native libraries allowed to be linked into the omni binary.
#
# omni ships as a self-contained binary, so every native library here is
# compiled into it. Adding an entry means accepting:
#
#   - a larger binary
#   - a C/C++ toolchain requirement for every cross-compiled target
#   - longer clean builds
#
# Enforced by .github/scripts/check-linked-libraries.sh, which reads the
# `cargo:rustc-link-lib=` directives emitted by build scripts. That catches
# statically linked libraries, which the finished binary cannot reveal --
# a static library leaves no DT_NEEDED entry behind.
#
# Format: "<crate> <kind>", one per line.
#
# Keyed on crate name and link kind rather than library name, because
# library names are not stable across versions or architectures:
#
#   aws-lc-sys      emits aws_lc_0_45_0_crypto, versioned in the name
#   blake3          emits blake3_neon on aarch64, blake3_sse2/avx2 on x86_64
#
# `kind` is normally `static`. A `dylib` or unspecified kind fails the check
# outright, whatever is listed here, since it would break self-sufficiency.
#
# Two exceptions exist on macOS, both OS-provided and both unavoidable:
#
#   `framework` entries are Apple system frameworks. They are always
#   dynamically linked and always present, so they do not threaten
#   self-sufficiency -- but they are still listed, so a NEW framework
#   dependency has to be reviewed.
#
#   libgit2-sys's `unspecified` iconv is hard-coded for apple targets and has
#   no static counterpart. See the note in check-linked-libraries.sh.
#
# Before adding an entry, consider whether the dependency can be avoided or
# replaced with a pure-Rust equivalent.

# rustls crypto backend, pulled in by reqwest's default features.
# Candidate for removal: see PLAN/01-binary-size.md item 3.
aws-lc-sys      static

# BLAKE3 SIMD implementation. Library name is architecture dependent.
blake3          static

# NOTE: there is deliberately no lzma entry. .tar.xz extraction uses the
# pure-Rust lzma-rust2 decoder, not a C binding. Static linkage of the old
# liblzma-sys was only ever enabled transitively by zip's `lzma-static`
# feature, so the zip 8 bump -- which switched zip to lzma-rust2 -- silently
# made it dynamic. Do not reintroduce a C lzma binding.

# libgit2. Deliberately retained rather than replaced by `git` subprocesses,
# because GitRepoEnv::new is on the shell prompt hot path.
# See PLAN/09-rejected.md
libgit2-sys     static

# SQLite, backing the omni cache.
libsqlite3-sys  static

# zlib. Required by libgit2-sys; the direct dependency in Cargo.toml exists
# only to force features=["static"].
libz-sys        static

# --- darwin only, below this line ---
#
# libgit2-sys links these three unconditionally for any apple target, in one
# block of its build.rs, alongside the static git2 above:
#
#     if target.contains("apple") {
#         println!("cargo:rustc-link-lib=iconv");
#         println!("cargo:rustc-link-lib=framework=Security");
#         println!("cargo:rustc-link-lib=framework=CoreFoundation");
#     }
#
# None of them are new; main links them too. They only became visible when
# this check first ran on darwin.
libgit2-sys     framework
libgit2-sys     unspecified

# SystemConfiguration, for reading macOS network/proxy settings. Pulled in by
# reqwest via system-configuration-sys. An OS framework, so dynamic and
# always present.
system-configuration-sys        framework
